<p>Five Italian citizens died on a deep cave scuba dive in the Maldives&#x27; Vaavu Atoll on Thursday, Italy&#x27;s Foreign Ministry said, in what Maldivian officials described as the country&#x27;s deadliest diving accident. Authorities had recovered one body and were searching for four others after the group failed to resurface from an underwater cave system at depths of about 50 to 60 meters. The victims included marine ecology professor Monica Montefalcone, her daughter Giorgia Sommacal, researchers Muriel Oddenino and Federico Gualtieri, and diving instructor Gianluca Benedetti, according to the University of Genoa and Italian media accounts. Four of the divers were linked to the University of Genoa, and the group was on a research or scientific tourism trip when the accident occurred. Maldivian authorities said the recovery operation was high-risk because of depth, currents and rough seas, and a dive by rescuers on Friday ended without finding the missing bodies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yzZBM59C9vdAuUQUjF5kePldKOUjcigmBcG4e_uelJ0HKQJgZbPRM9n1sobo1SIkbGfZX50oZPWbWkto0voC0HozcGctAbjMymT9nu7kX53ytF-Wi5-tq7AnIgwZkDz1MyhGxk1vT7lS-yc6zjFo_IwWe26QNluxGJQ1I9f4DjmOIix-lfr65lisv_oNnVqg7fGgLiaoX6MEgVukFikjEVcvAc6RxP3gbjCbCNjggaSRwn1R3tWCFI6Dcw5F5O0nrv8BqQ7KydAVMII' alt='The Italian divers who disappeared and were later declared dead in the Maldives.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Diver experience: Italian reports described the five as experienced divers rather than novice tourists.</li><li>Victim origins: RAI reported the victims were from Genoa, Padua, Milan, Novara and Turin.</li><li>Cave layout: The cave was described as having three connected sections, and Italian diplomatic officials said divers had explored two before a later attempt to reach the third.</li><li>Recovered body: Italian reports identified the body recovered from the cave as diving instructor Gianluca Benedetti.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Maldives National Defence Force: The MNDF said aircraft, speedboats and a coastguard vessel joined the initial response after the divers were reported overdue. (<a href='https://www.letemps.ch/articles/cinq-italiens-meurent-dans-un-accident-de-plongee-aux-maldives'>Le Temps</a>, <a href='https://www.iltempo.it/attualita/2026/05/15/news/maldive-recuperato-grotta-corpo-sub-meteo-squali-ricerche-cause-tragedia-47744121/'>Il Tempo</a>)</li><li>Italian Foreign Ministry: The ministry said the circumstances of the accident were still unclear and that Maldivian authorities were responsible for establishing what happened. (<a href='https://www.dhakatribune.com/world/europe/410284/ministry-five-italians-die-in-scuba-accident-in'>Dhaka Tribune</a>)</li><li>University of Genoa: The university said the deaths were a loss for its marine-science community after identifying several victims among its faculty, family members and researchers. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tourists-killed-maldives-cave-diving-accident-italy/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Rome prosecutors: Italian judicial authorities opened a file in Rome while Maldivian authorities pursued the local inquiry. (<a href='https://www.kathimerini.gr/world/564228823/italia-eisaggeliki-ereyna-gia-ton-thanato-ton-pente-italon-dyton-stis-maldives/'>Kathimerini</a>, <a href='https://www.rtl.it/notizie/articoli/roma-ha-avviato-un-indagine-sull-incidente-verificatosi-durante-l-immersione-in-una-grotta/'>RTL</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/article/3353751/maldives-rescuers-search-missing-italian-divers-underwater-cave'>Maldives rescuers search for missing Italian divers in underwater cave</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/authorities-search-waters-maldives-after-5-italians-killed-132994343'>Search in waters off the Maldives for bodies of Italians killed in cave dive accident</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tourists-killed-maldives-cave-di